      // count for that (user, date) — the local row always knows
      // the total launches up to this moment. Remote was the
      // cumulative count at the previous push. SUM was inflating
      // single-machine multi-push scenarios: push 1 → 1+0=1,
      // push 2 (no new activity) → 1+1=2, push 3 → 1+2=3, … the
      // count grew on every push regardless of actual launches.
      // MAX gives the right answer for same-machine cumulative
      // pushes AND for multi-machine where the higher count
      // dominates (a user with 50 launches from one machine + 5
      // from another reports as 50, not 55 — slightly
      // undercounting cross-machine but never inflating).
